{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SzLKc1C9SNdz6NWCpMEkmH","type":"tool_result","content":"745\t### A3.5 What this amendment does NOT decide\n746\t\n747\t- Migrating any `veto_floor: true` agent file off `claude-fable-5`.\n748\t- `_lib/model_routing.py` `_ROUTING_TABLE` (debate/arch stay on\n749\t  `claude-opus-5`), the reviewer default in `check_codex_stop_review.py`,\n750\t  and the `hooks/_lib/tier_policy` `MODEL_ID` enum.\n751\t- Prices beyond the rate card (A3.1). The same derived patch gives the\n752\t  $4/$20 row to `cost-table.yaml` and to every cost-rollup table that\n753\t  `test_model_fleet_presence.py` binds to this ADR's working set, and\n754\t  0.05x to the two per-model cache-read tables that test holds equal.\n755\t  Per-model price tables outside that oracle (Owner-provenance snapshots,\n756\t  drift fixtures, research and tournament instruments, the tier-policy\n757\t  cost gate) are not changed. The rollups that look a model up by its\n758\t  exact spelling do not price the `[1m]`-tagged spelling of\n759\t  `claude-opus-5-5`.\n760\t- The `upgrade.sh` T3.4 gate that withholds the DirectoryAdded /\n761\t  Notification registrations from adopter settings: A3.2 item 11 raises\n762\t  the adopter floor to Claude Code 2.1.280 but leaves that gate OFF.\n763\t- `SPEC/v1/install-cli.md`: it lists neither `--allow-old-claude-code`,\n764\t  nor `--adopt-setting`, nor exit 6. Its exit-code table already lags the\n765\t  scripts (it stops at 3, while its own flag table names exits 4 and 5);\n766\t  the SPEC is not changed here.\n767\t- `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/team.md` and the CHANGELOG (closeout and release\n768\t  surfaces).\n769\t\n770\tThe A1.1 sentence on the primary session model and A2.2 item 4 are\n771\thistorical; the session pin is `claude-opus-5-5` (A3.2 item 4).\n772\t\n773\t## Amendment 4 — PLAN-176 semantic families (2026-11-01, Onda 6B)\n774\t\n775\tThe Owner authorizes family admission without a GPG ceremony for each model version.\n776\tThe earlier closed-list/per-bump clauses remain historical; this amendment replaces them.\n777\t\n778\t# MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY = \"semantic-families-v1\"\n779\t\n780\tThe explicit blocks remain deterministic compatibility mirrors. Their historic A2/A3 tail\n781\tis retained; new compatible identifiers do not need another entry or signature. Runtime\n782\tacceptance is explicit membership OR an anchored family: Claude opus/sonnet/haiku majors\n783\t4–9, GPT 5–9, o 3–9, Gemini 2–9, Grok 3–9. Only Opus, GPT and o families, plus the\n784\texplicit legacy floor, are VETO-eligible. Sonnet, Haiku, Gemini and Grok availability"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d0a8a2c-572f-4c52-9f2d-9f32350c1173","uuid":"28b6b1d4-5724-4335-8a55-0a87df9ede7b","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:41:47.517Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-149-model-id-allowlist.md","content":"### A3.5 What this amendment does NOT decide\n\n- Migrating any `veto_floor: true` agent file off `claude-fable-5`.\n- `_lib/model_routing.py` `_ROUTING_TABLE` (debate/arch stay on\n  `claude-opus-5`), the reviewer default in `check_codex_stop_review.py`,\n  and the `hooks/_lib/tier_policy` `MODEL_ID` enum.\n- Prices beyond the rate card (A3.1). The same derived patch gives the\n  $4/$20 row to `cost-table.yaml` and to every cost-rollup table that\n  `test_model_fleet_presence.py` binds to this ADR's working set, and\n  0.05x to the two per-model cache-read tables that test holds equal.\n  Per-model price tables outside that oracle (Owner-provenance snapshots,\n  drift fixtures, research and tournament instruments, the tier-policy\n  cost gate) are not changed. The rollups that look a model up by its\n  exact spelling do not price the `[1m]`-tagged spelling of\n  `claude-opus-5-5`.\n- The `upgrade.sh` T3.4 gate that withholds the DirectoryAdded /\n  Notification registrations from adopter settings: A3.2 item 11 raises\n  the adopter floor to Claude Code 2.1.280 but leaves that gate OFF.\n- `SPEC/v1/install-cli.md`: it lists neither `--allow-old-claude-code`,\n  nor `--adopt-setting`, nor exit 6. Its exit-code table already lags the\n  scripts (it stops at 3, while its own flag table names exits 4 and 5);\n  the SPEC is not changed here.\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/team.md` and the CHANGELOG (closeout and release\n  surfaces).\n\nThe A1.1 sentence on the primary session model and A2.2 item 4 are\nhistorical; the session pin is `claude-opus-5-5` (A3.2 item 4).\n\n## Amendment 4 — PLAN-176 semantic families (2026-11-01, Onda 6B)\n\nThe Owner authorizes family admission without a GPG ceremony for each model version.\nThe earlier closed-list/per-bump clauses remain historical; this amendment replaces them.\n\n# MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY = \"semantic-families-v1\"\n\nThe explicit blocks remain deterministic compatibility mirrors. Their historic A2/A3 tail\nis retained; new compatible identifiers do not need another entry or signature. Runtime\nacceptance is explicit membership OR an anchored family: Claude opus/sonnet/haiku majors\n4–9, GPT 5–9, o 3–9, Gemini 2–9, Grok 3–9. Only Opus, GPT and o families, plus the\nexplicit legacy floor, are VETO-eligible. Sonnet, Haiku, Gemini and Grok availability","numLines":40,"startLine":745,"totalLines":797}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SzLKc1C9SNdz6NWCpMEkmH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
