turns a deny. An exception reaches the hook's outer FATAL handler.\n  * The redactor ingress condition and \"scheduled for the next release\" (CHANGELOG:418-422).\n  * No branch protection (CHANGELOG:148).\n  * The \"Version number.\" paragraph (CHANGELOG:72).\n- The model-family changes in this payload (generate-available-models.py and the model-deprecations.json exemptions) fall inside the declared cond 9.\nNo declared condition is false against this payload.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1. The facade moves preserve behavior, the Python stays standard-library only and 3.9-compatible, and the only shipped scripts touched are lessons.py, context-budget.py, generate-available-models.py, gen-command-skill-hook-map.py, derive-audit-family.py and diagnose-output-hook.py. None of them is a hook, none fails closed on an infrastructure fault, and none writes outside its place.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2 — .claude/scripts/local/pair-rail-gate.sh:180-181, 196-198, 241-242 (stale comments).\n   Failure: the comments still say Gate 3b runs codex \"ONLY after Gate 4 verified the payload sha\" and that exit 0 means \"verified\". The compatible arm now reaches the `codex --version` exec with no hash attestation. The runtime INFO line at :231 is honest; the comments are not.\n   Fix: reword them to \"after Gate 4 returned verified or version-floor compatible (not hash-verified)\".\n2. P2 — .claude/scripts/local/mac_sign_and_release.py:130 (automatic attestation), plus :16 and :113 (single-use constants).\n   Failure: cut_release always passes --npm-readme-reviewed to release.sh bump and only prints a reminder. That flag is a deliberate human tripwire (release.sh:58-61, 564-567), so the wrapper turns an attestation into a no-op. TRACK and the \"Merge pull request #7\" message are hard-coded: running sign-merge on a later train would produce a merge commit that names the wrong pull request. The script is maintainer-only; install.sh copies only top-level .claude/scripts/*.py.\n   Fix: require an explicit --npm-readme-reviewed (or an interactive confirmation) on the wrapper and forward it. Take the track and PR number as required arguments.\n3. P2 — .claude/scripts/gen-command-skill-hook-map.py:205-219.\n   Failure: the binder map ignores the package= keyword. For check_agent_spawn.py:128-129 (install(globals(), ..., package=\"_lib.agent_spawn\")) the generator scans _lib/_audit_emit_parts/ instead of _lib/agent_spawn/. The map is right today only because the facade itself contains \"SKILL.md\" (3 hits). Also, :201 dropped errors=\"replace\", so a hook that is not UTF-8 now crashes the generator.\n   Fix: when a binder call carries a package= keyword whose value is a string constant, use it. Restore errors=\"replace\".\n4. P2 — .claude/scripts/generate-available-models.py:48-58 and :118-120.\n   Failure (a): if the _lib.model_currency import fails, the lambda fallback silently drops the family prefixes. --check then reports \"drift\" (exit 1) for what is really an infrastructure fault (exit 2).\n   Failure (b): the prefix branch never fires against the shipped ADR. ADR-149:778 writes the marker as a Markdown heading (\"# MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY = ...\"), outside any python fence, so _POLICY_FENCE_RE never matches. The MODEL_FAMILY_POLICY constant at :54 is unused. If someone later moves the marker into a fence, the generated availableModels gains gpt-/o-/gemini-/grok- prefixes and --check goes red against .claude/settings.json:797-806.\n   Fix: on ImportError, return 2 when the fence is present. Remove or test the unused branch, and state in ADR-149 or the docstring that the mirror stays explicit.\n5. P2 — .claude/scripts/model-deprecations.json:366-368.\n   Failure: the model-currency-family-prefixes exemption now covers all of _lib/model_currency.py. Its reason text describes a \"_FAMILIES table\" of vendor prefixes, but that file holds full ids: claude-opus-4-1 in _RETIRED, and claude-fable-5 and claude-fable-5-1 in _LEGACY_WORKING. _LEGACY_WORKING admits ids, so a retired id added there later would escape the deprecation scanner. This falls under cond 9 in substance; the reason string is inaccurate.\n   Fix: narrow the exemption to the _RETIRED and _PREFIXES lines, or correct the reason text.\n6. P2 — .claude/scripts/context-budget.py:199 and the module docstring (lines 62-64).\n   Failure: the new import, `from _lib._context_budget_parts import install`, is not guarded. If _lib cannot be imported, this advisory CLI exits with a traceback (non-zero), although the docstring promises \"always 0\", and the earlier degraded mode becomes unreachable (the \"DEGRADED: _lib/injection_patterns unavailable\" note). _context_budget_parts/inventory.py:14-15 also re-declares CHARS_PER_TOKEN and REDACTED to build HONESTY_NOTES, a second copy that can drift from the facade.\n   Fix: guard the install and print a degraded message with exit 0. Have HONESTY_NOTES read the facade constants.\n7. P2 — the two binders diverge: _lib/_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48, which lessons.py:204-206 reuses through package=, versus _lib/_context_budget_parts/__init__.py:27-52.\n   Failure: only the context-budget binder rebinds classes. A class added later to _lessons_parts would keep its part module's globals, and every facade name would raise NameError when called.\n   Fix: give lessons its own _lessons_parts.install, or move one shared binder that handles classes into _lib.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Every declared condition this payload touches (3a, 7, 10, 11, 12 and the cond 9 model-family surface) holds against the code, the facade moves keep their behavior, adopter-facing paths stay fail-open, and the payload has no P0 and no new P1, only seven P2 follow-ups."},"ttft_ms":26326,"type":"result","duration_ms":493201,"uuid":"f2c5e565-65db-4cf8-a189-5cfa02ee1265","ttft_stream_ms":5133,"time_to_request_ms":175,"first_content_frame_ms":5133,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude